      <gmd:lineage>
        <gmd:LI_Lineage>
          <gmd:statement>
            <gco:CharacterString>For Dominant Leaf Type (DLT), temporal convolutional neural networks have been trained for biogeographically strata (production units) on Sentinel-2 time-series for all reference years ± 3 months. The training data has been derived from LUCAS 2018, existing CLMS products and through interpretation of VHR imagery and Sentinel-2 time series. Post-classification processing steps include spatial and temporal filtering to assure a high consistencyof the time series while preserving acutal land cover changes. Thematic target accuracy: 90% producer and user accuracy.

This dataset is a continuation of the HRL Dominant Leaf Type timeseries, previously generated on a 3-year update cycle since 2012. The models and input data used to generate the product have evolved and therefore higher quality is to be expected as the timeseries progress.

Quality assurance follows the ISO9000 standards for Quality Management and comprises of dedicated procedures of ongoing quality checks (QA breakpoints) during implementation of the production chain, in order to keep persistent control over the various stages of production, assure fitness-for-purpose of the end-products and that all quality requirements are fulfilled. Priority has been given to the target thematic accuracies to be achieved by each product, as well as to the issues of product consistency (spatial, thematic, temporal) and homogeneity. Quality Assessment: The quality assessment has been performed according to INSPIRE Data Specifications. The data quality elements considered are:
(i) Completeness,
(ii) Logical Consistency,
(iii) Thematic Accuracy,
(iv) Temporal quality and
(v) Usability.
Each of them (excl. the Thematic Accuracy hereafter) forms a section in the QA/QC Procedures.</gco:CharacterString>
          </gmd:statement>
        </gmd:LI_Lineage>
      </gmd:lineage>
    </gmd:DQ_DataQuality>
